    "created_at": "2016-06-06T17:07:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-06T17:07:44Z",
    "body": "> If we group things by functions, observedAttributes has no value if attributeChangedCallback is not set, and the reverse if also true, correct? I didn't do in my WIP yet but it could be a possible optimization not to Get() one if the other does not exist.\n\nThat's very interesting. How about I change it so that it's roughly:\n1. Let observedAttributes be an empty `sequence<DOMString>`.\n2. Get attributeChangedCallback\n3. If attributeChangedCallback is not undefined,\n   1. If IsCallable(attributeChangedCallback) is false, throw a TypeError.\n   2. Get observedAttributesIterable, and convert it and store it in observedAttributes.\n\n> I'm not too strong either, but if the order doesn't matter, maybe it's nice to say impls can do these things in different order?\n\nUnfortunately that leads to web-observabled differences. We might be able to get away with them for edge cases like this, but it's better to avoid them and have the spec mandate a single behavior which everyone follows.\n",
